So, Its been a very long time since we ventured out on a Tuesday afternoon with the van jam packed with drums ready for drum and dance classes. The drums have been stored away and the van has remained empty for almost all of the entire time. There was one sunny day when we treated them all to some lovely sunshine and a good scrub, but other than that, class drums have remained very lonely and hands and feet have continued to soften...Its time to blow out those COVID-19 cobwebs and kilos!

**NEW THINGS IN CLASS**

We are hoping that restrictions keep easing and there is no backwards from here on in. Classes will look a little different with 1.5metre spacing for both drum and dance. Please keep chairs where they are and remain in your lines for dancing. We will also have hand sanitiser at the front entrance of the hall for everyone to use. Please keep social distancing when entering the hall and paying for your class. We would love to have a chat with each and everyone of you, but to keep things organised we just need to get everyone through the door first.

**WORKING TOGETHER**

Unfortunately, these are the guidelines at the moment and we need to do the right thing to avoid being shut down and of course your health and ours is top priority. If everyone can remain conscious about these things, that will be amazing and make our evening so much easier.

**Time and Date**

Class times will remain the same with beginners/experienced class at 5.30pm and open dance 6.30pm.

See you all Tuesday 14th July!

Bec and Nat
